# Title: Regsvr32 Execution From Potential Suspicious Location
# ID: 9525dc73-0327-438c-8c04-13c0e037e9da
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2023-05-26
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.t1218.010
# Description: Detects execution of regsvr32 where the DLL is located in a potentially suspicious location.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((process.command_line:*:\\ProgramData\\* OR process.command_line:*:\\Temp\\* OR process.command_line:*:\\Users\\Public\\* OR process.command_line:*:\\Windows\\Temp\\* OR process.command_line:*\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\* OR process.command_line:*\\AppData\\Roaming\\*)) AND ((process.executable:*\\regsvr32.exe) OR (process.pe.original_file_name:"REGSVR32.EXE")))
